quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  40,78,"We have sent (many) messengers before you. Among them are some We have recounted to you, and some among them We have not recounted to you. And it was not for any messenger to bring any sign except by Allah’s permission. So when Allah’s command comes, judgement will be passed with justice. And those who make false claims will thence become losers."
  40,79,"Allah is the One Who made cattle for you; some of them you ride, and some of them you eat."
  40,80,"And there are (other) benefits for you in them—that, riding upon them, you may reach the destination (desired) in your hearts. And you are carried upon them and the ships (on your journeys)."
  40,81,"And He shows you (many of) His signs. So, which of Allah’s signs will you deny?"
  40,82,Have they not travelled throughout the land so that they could observe what was the end of those before them? They were more numerous than them and were far mightier in power (than these pagans) and (richer) in the monumental marks (they left) in the land. But whatever they used to earn brought them no benefit.
  40,83,"So when their messengers came to them with clear proofs, they rejoiced in pride for whatever (worldly) knowledge they had. So (the torment) which they used to ridicule overtook them."
  40,84,"But when they saw Our punishment, they said: ‘We believe in Allah alone and reject what we had been associating with Him (as partners).’"
  40,85,"But their belief could not profit them when they had seen Our punishment. Allah’s practice has always passed among His (defiant) servants (like this), and the disbelievers were, hence, at a total loss."
